### Topic 62 - Config Server
### Start: config-server (8888) -> product-service (8081)

### ---------- Ask the Config Server directly ----------

### 1. Config for product-service, default profile (JSON: a list of property sources)
GET http://localhost:8888/product-service/default

### 2. Config for product-service, dev profile (dev file listed FIRST = highest priority)
GET http://localhost:8888/product-service/dev

### 3. The merged result as a YAML file
GET http://localhost:8888/product-service-dev.yml

### 4. Encrypt a secret (paste the result into config-repo as '{cipher}<result>')
POST http://localhost:8888/encrypt
Content-Type: text/plain

my-super-secret

### ---------- The client: product-service ----------

### 5. Where did my values come from? (welcome message, company, profile)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/message

### 6. Prices with the centrally configured discount
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products

### 7. Feature flag: 404 by default, works with the dev profile
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/new-arrivals

### 8. Did we receive the decrypted secret? (masked)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/secret-check

### 9. LIVE RELOAD: edit config-repo/product-service.yml, save, then:
POST http://localhost:8081/actuator/refresh

### 10. ...and check again (beanCreatedAt changes because of @RefreshScope)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/message

### 11. DEV ONLY: see every property and the file it came from
GET http://localhost:8081/actuator/env/shop.discount-percent
